<title>UKRAINE: Ukraine March inflation 0.1 pct vs 1.2 pct Feb.</title>
<headline>Ukraine March inflation 0.1 pct vs 1.2 pct Feb.</headline>
<dateline>KIEV 1997-04-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ukraine's monthly inflation slowed to 0.1 percent in March, from 1.2 percent in February, Finance Minister Ihor Mityukov told reporters on Thursday.</p>
<p>    UKRAINE CONSUMER PRICES    MAR 97   FEB 97   MAR 96</p>
<p>    month-on-month pct change  +0.1     +1.2     +3.0</p>
<p>Mityukov did not provide year-on-year figures.</p>
<p>Ukraine has forecast annual inflation at 25 percent in 1997 after 39.7 percent last year.</p>
<p>It last achieved monthly inflation levels of 0.1 percent in June and July of 1996.</p>
<p>--Irene Marushko, Kiev Newsroom +380 44 244-9150</p>
</text>
